Code:

Comparator<Integer> c = (a, b) -> b - a; // max-heap

PriorityQueue<Integer> pq = new PriorityQueue<>(c);

Step1: Comparator<Integer> c

This creates a Comparator named c.

A Comparator tells Java: "When you compare two integers, use this rule to decide their order."

Step2: (a, b) -> b - a

This is a lambda expression that defines the comparison rule.

Here:

a = first number
b = second number
b - a = comparison rule

It means larger numbers should come before smaller numbers.

For example:

a = 10
b = 30

b - a

30 - 10 = positive

This makes 30 come before 10.

So the order becomes: 30 → 20 → 10

That's why it creates a max-heap behavior.